    <statement><p>Find the linearization <m>L \left( x, y \right)</m> of the function <m>f\left( x,
y \right) = \sqrt{ 109 - 9 x^{2} - 16 y^{2} }</m> at <m>\left( -2, -2 \right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>L \left( x, y \right) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answer should be an expression in x and y; e.g. <lq/>3x - 5y + 9<rq/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6\mathopen{}\left(x-\left(-2\right)\right)+10.6667\mathopen{}\left(y-\left(-2\right)\right)+3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
